course: dictionary
lesson: 3734
title: Floodplains: flat land beside a river
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A floodplain is flat land beside a river. Its name gives you a clue: flood means water covering land, and plain means flat land. «A floodplain is the flat land beside a river that is covered with water when the river floods.» So when the river floods, the water spreads out over the floodplain.
explain: Try the meaning in a sentence: «The farm sits on the floodplain.» Does it make sense that a farm is on flat land next to a river? Yes, so the meaning fits. Always check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
explain: Floodplains can be good for farming. When the water goes down, it leaves behind mud called silt, and silt makes the soil rich. But floodplains are also risky, because a house built there may be flooded. So people must think carefully before they build on a floodplain.
fact: A floodplain is flat land beside a river.
fact: A floodplain is covered with water when the river floods.
fact: A flood is a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry.
fact: Floods leave mud called silt, which makes the soil fertile, so it is good for growing crops.
fact: Building on a floodplain is risky because the houses can be flooded.
exercise: «A floodplain is the flat land beside a river that is covered with water when the river floods.» What is a floodplain? | A deep lake high in the mountains | A steep hill far away from any river | *Flat land beside a river that gets covered with water when it floods | A road built over a river
exercise: Why are floodplains good for farming? | The land is too steep for crops to grow | *Floods leave mud called silt, which makes the soil fertile | Rivers never flood there | Floods wash all the soil away for ever
exercise: Which two words join together to make floodplain? | flood and river | *flood and plain | river and land | rain and plain
test: Why is it risky to build houses on a floodplain? | The houses are too high to be seen from the river | Nothing, it is always safe | The houses will sink into the mud for ever | *The houses may be flooded when the river rises
test: «Farmers like floodplains because the soil is fertile.» What does fertile mean here? | Covered in ice | Very steep and rocky | *Good for growing plants | Hard as rock
exam: Ayesha says a floodplain is a steep mountain. What is a floodplain, and what is wrong with her idea? | *It is flat land beside a river, not a steep mountain | It is always under the sea | It is a mountain beside the sea | She is right, a floodplain is a steep mountain
